# Nouns that count people or things a clock never takes: a bare hour behind a
# clock preposition and directly before one of them is a count ("wave at 5
# people").  Each word is quoted from its Wiktionary Noun entry
# (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/<word>); the fetched pages are kept with the audit.
# pessoa: Noun. "person an individual being, especially a human"
# pessoas: Noun. "plural of pessoa"
# vizinhos: Noun. "plural of vizinho"
# vizinhas: Noun. "plural of vizinha"
# amigos: Noun. "plural of amigo"
# amigas: Noun. "plural of amiga"
# crianças: Noun. "plural of criança"
# meninos: Noun. "plural of menino"
# meninas: Noun. "plural of menina"
# rapazes: Noun. "plural of rapaz"
# raparigas: Noun. "plural of rapariga"
# adultos: Noun. "plural of adulto"
# jogadores: Noun. "plural of jogador"
# jogadoras: Noun. "plural of jogadora"
# lugares: Noun. "plural of lugar"
# mesas: Noun. "plural of mesa"
# bilhetes: Noun. "plural of bilhete"
# quartos: Noun. "quarterfinals"
# alunos: Noun. "plural of aluno"
# alunas: Noun. "plural of aluna"
# primos: Noun. "plural of primo"
# primas: Noun. "plural of prima"
# gatos: Noun. "plural of gato"
# gatas: Noun. "plural of gata"
pessoa
pessoas
